Subject: [PATCH 20/49] mobile: an opt-in log of the iOS keyboard's edits
 (diagnostics)

The Korean fix diffs the hidden field once it settles, with timings and
guards taken from upstream fixtures, not from the edit sequences a given iOS
version produces. When typing still goes wrong on a device, those sequences
are what is needed to fix it.

A long press on the keyboard button starts a log of the last 60 field changes
(time, filler length, the text after it, selection and composing range) and
the edits sent for them; the next long press shows it with Copy, Stop and
Close. It is off by default, kept in memory only and cleared by Stop; it
holds what was typed. iOS only; it is one self-contained patch so a release
can leave it out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
